 "description": "species of bird",
 "extract": "The whiskered tern (Chlidonias hybrida) is a  tern in the family Laridae. The genus name is from Ancient Greek khelidonios, \"swallow-like\", from khelidon, \"swallow\". The specific hybridus is Latin for hybrid; Peter Simon Pallas thought it might be a hybrid of white-winged black tern and common tern, writing \"Sterna fissipes [Chlidonias leucopterus] et Hirundine [Sterna hirundo] natam\".",
